  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to the de-Broglie hypothesis according to which all matters have both particle and wave nature. where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo></math> plank's constant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>=</mo></math>momentum, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>=</mo></math> wavelength of particle. This type of graph is called a rectangular hyperbola. As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mfrac></math> we will have a rectangular hyperbola.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> (constant)</p><p>So, the plot is a rectangular hyperbola.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0040_8a64b0021cf5.png\" style=\"width: 196px; height: 200px;\"/></p>"
